  "_comment": "AUTHORITATIVE shared fixtures for the Wallet Security Suite (docs/WALLET-SECURITY.md §5). IDENTICAL across blockle-extension/security.js (JS, reference — authored these), blockle-app/lib (Dart), python/blockle (Python). Every money value is a base-unit decimal string (BigInt-exact). ctxSpec carries PLAIN data only (no functions) so every language builds the same injected ctx from it: codeByAddress maps a spender address to its on-chain code ('0x' or '' => EOA, no code); balances maps asset symbol -> base units; usd maps asset symbol -> USD price (a symbol absent from the map resolves to null => mismatch-currency); seenRecipients / priorApprovals are local-history sets. EVM addresses compare case-insensitively (decode lowercases them). 'warnings' in each expect is the SORTED set of warning codes that must fire; severity is the max over them.",
